Metal path, kernel side: host-memory import (0x49) and the Metal plug-in names (spesmetal=1).

metal2vulkan requires VK_EXT_external_memory_host, which Turnip's drm layer (iOSPlus10 negronigl
drm) builds on request 0x49: a buffer over the caller's own pages. Ported from iOSPlus10 0232 onto
our RedwoodGPU: the pages are wired and mapped for the kernel, pushed out of the cache at import
and before every submission that names them, never kept for reuse, waited for and unwired on free;
clientMemoryForType refuses them (the program has its own mapping).

Boot-arg spesmetal=1 names iOSPlus10's NegroniMetal plug-in on IOAcceleratorES (MetalPluginName,
MetalPluginClassName), which Metal.framework's device registration reads. Off by default.

